[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3353022553","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110895#issuecomment-3353022553","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110895","id":3353022553,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7H2xBZ","user":{"login":"lostminds","id":17763524,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzYzNTI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17763524?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds","html_url":"https://github.com/lostminds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-30T16:47:33Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T16:47:33Z","body":"I think some sort of setting like this is a very important addition from a UI/UX perspective after the changes in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110250 . As I understand it that PR changed things to make it easier to avoid showing unwanted focus rings around buttons when you're not using keyboard/controller navigation. But this misses the other big use of focus highlights of controls to show the user where keyboard entry or other secondary editing is currently directed (as in what text field you're currently editing, what color well is active when picking a color or other similar custom input controls). For these cases I think it's expected and needed for the control to get and show focus when clicked with a mouse, and unfortunate if this current functionality would break in 4.6.\r\n\r\nIf I understand it correctly however, this PR would only add a possible exception for TextEdit and LineEdit explicitly, so it won't be possible to use for custom Controls where you want or may be relying on the old behavior?\r\n\r\nPerhaps this whole showing focus behavior could be handled better via something like the [control focus modes](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_control.html#enum-control-focusmode) instead, allowing to set the behavior per control with a default rather than project wide with project settings like this?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3353022553/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3353148577","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110895#issuecomment-3353148577","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110895","id":3353148577,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7H3Pyh","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-30T17:24:09Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T17:24:09Z","body":"> If I understand it correctly however, this PR would only add a possible exception for TextEdit and LineEdit explicitly, so it won't be possible to use for custom Controls where you want or may be relying on the old behavior?\r\n\r\nWhether a custom `Control` shows focus or not depends entirely on you. Hidden focus is only ignored if you use `has_focus()` with `true`, so if you want your `Control` to always show it, you still can.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3353148577/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3353250256","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110895#issuecomment-3353250256","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110895","id":3353250256,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7H3onQ","user":{"login":"lostminds","id":17763524,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzYzNTI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17763524?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds","html_url":"https://github.com/lostminds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-30T17:58:18Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T17:58:18Z","body":"> Whether a custom `Control` shows focus or not depends entirely on you. Hidden focus is only ignored if you use `has_focus()` with `true`, so if you want your `Control` to always show it, you still can.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure I follow, I assume the engine would call `has_focus()` with `true` in this case to determine if it should show the focus ring? And as it's a built in class method `has_focus` can't be overriden to change what it returns in my custom control class. Say I have a custom control inheriting Button that brings up some selection interface (like a color picker). Currently if I set this to `focus_mode` ALL it will get a focus ring when it is clicked, which is what I want. This will also disappear as expected when changing focus to some other control. But as I understand it this will no longer happen after https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110250 (with default project settings) as the control received focus with from a mouse click, which will not be shown?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3353250256/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3353303470","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110895#issuecomment-3353303470","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110895","id":3353303470,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7H31mu","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"h